## Why This Is Asked
Tests for onboarding across regions and async services are common in fintech; this question probes end-to-end reliability, data isolation, and failure handling.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end testing with external dependencies
- Event-driven architecture and eventual consistency
- Data isolation and idempotency
- Regional failure scenarios and recovery
- Test determinism via mocks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright skeleton: intercept KYC and mock responses; drive onboarding flow
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';
test('onboarding E2E with mocked KYC and event bus', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/kyc/*', r => r.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ ok: true }) }));
  await page.route('**/event-bus/*', r => r.fulfill({ status: 202 }));
  await page.goto('https://fintech.example/onboard');
  await page.fill('#email','user@example.com');
  await page.click('#submit');
  await expect(page.locator('#status')).toHaveText(/pending|kyc_passed|approved/);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale this to thousands of concurrent onboarding flows?
- How would you validate idempotency across multiple regions and tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests RBAC in a realistic multi-tenant admin UI with progressive permission changes, ensuring isolation and correct UI cues.

## Key Concepts
- RBAC policies per-tenant
- Test data seeding and isolation
- UI visibility vs. API enforcement
- Role upgrade propagation without relogin

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright example sketch
test('RBAC per-tenant role upgrade', async ({ page }) => {
  await loginAsTenantUser(page, 'TenantA', 'u1', 'viewer');
  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/dashboard/);
  await expect(page.locator('#user-management')).toBeHidden();
  await upgradeRole(page, 'TenantA', 'u1', 'editor');
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('#user-management')).toBeVisible();
  await loginAsTenantUser(page, 'TenantB', 'u2', 'viewer');
  await expect(page.locator('#tenant-data')).toHaveText(/TenantA/).toBeHidden();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle flaky network affecting role-change propagation? 
- What assertions would you add to guard against stale caches after role changes?

